obviously you i don't believe you've  been picked up for season three yet but  how much are you already thinking about  season three and what you want to  accomplish  uh at this point we are  maybe two thirds of the way shooting  season two um and still in the midst of  writing that i haven't finished writing  season two yet i have spent  zero  time thinking about about season three  i am  scrambling to keep my head above water  in season two  have not thought of it one bit to be on  i mean  that's not a hundred percent true  actually because  so you were live in the interview i get  it i get it no no the truth is as you  arch out these characters and we we are  in the process of working out like  what's the end of season two you have to  have some awareness of do we really want  to end them here because then season  three if we get one would be like this  we don't want to do that so you have a  bit of an awareness of like  what might be a good setup for for a  season three what might not be without  really knowing what the details of  season three might be but you do  there is an awareness in the room now  that we talk about it of  what's the jumping off point in the  season three because that's where you're  ending them in season two and is this  where we want to end harry in season two  because if we do that means season three  will be this and is that  am i going to get to season three and  say god i wish we hadn't done that so  there's an awareness of it you want to  set yourself up for success in the next  season so you want to end the characters  in an exciting fun place so that you  have  you know again without knowing what the  details would be in the future at least  you have a general sense of like oh that  could be cool to explore that in a new  season  i'm assuming season two is ten episodes  uh season two is not ten episodes season  two  is uh is more than ten episodes we did  ten last year we uh the season the first  half of season two is eight episodes  i think the plan is  a lot depends on covet you know but it's  split into two halves the first half  will be eight the second half i think  hopefully will be eight um  it's a weird world right now so there's  no guarantees of what's going to happen  but the plan is to do  is to do 16.  knowing that it was supposed to be 16  episodes did you write episode 8 as a  almost mini finale  yes  yeah it was a it was  the most difficult part of this season  um  structurally was going from a 10 episode  season to a longer season and it's a  different thing it's not you know 10 is  there's a reason that these cable shows  compress there's there's so much more  going on in 10 episodes the problem you  have more episodes is you run the risk  of treading water for a while  so what we tried to do was split that  chunk if we are we do do 16 split it  into halves  and then the first eight would build to  a mid-season finale  that would you know be a bit of a  cliffhanger but not like the end of the  season but and we do have a good one so  the first eight does have a bit of a  cliffhanger and then the second eight  builds  um  to something you know even bigger  uh and and but thematically both halves  are  are connected the the character arcs  although they may be arced out for each  half the overall arc of each character  spans the whole amount of time so it's  very tricky to do but i think we we  figured it out  i i have to stop i'm uh because they  they gave me the thing but i'll just say  that i uh uh yeah if you're doing eight  episodes and you just you're writing it  almost like as a mini season you know  but yeah  everything's going  everything's going crazy thank you so  much i really enjoy the show thanks  steve appreciate it

